ORI SharpHound relationship-contract hardening

Purpose
- Prevent planted and supporting relationships from existing only in ORI's internal graph or manifest while disappearing from serialized SharpHound data or the live BloodHound CE graph.
- Establish one canonical relationship vocabulary across generation, serialization, manifests, ingest verification, direct grading, and MCP grading.

Relationship contract
- Adds src/ori/relationships.py as the centralized registry for canonical relationship names, endpoint types, SharpHound carriers, wire values, live CE kinds, and support classification.
- Canonicalizes WriteDACL to WriteDacl and legacy TrustedBy to SameForestTrust at explicit compatibility boundaries.
- Rejects unknown relationship kinds and noncanonical SharpHound ACE rights instead of silently dropping them.
- Preserves trust direction when reconstructing ParentChild trust relationships.

Generation and archive validation
- Centralizes graph-edge projection into SharpHound structures.
- Validates every planted path edge and supporting edge against the completed ZIP before writing it.
- Keeps contextual Enroll and SameForestTrust evidence separate from continuous path edges.
- Confirms the complex seed-4401 corpus contains all 30 planted paths at the archive boundary.

Manifest and CLI contract
- Emits ori-generated-manifest-v2.
- Records relationship-contract version, SharpHound encoding profile and per-file versions, and the tested/supported BloodHound CE 9.1.0 baseline.
- Records projected counts for all 12 SharpHound file/object categories and reconciles them with total projected nodes.
- Labels total_edges as internal graph edges and adds an archive-derived canonical relationship-count ledger.
- Accepts direct as the public track name while retaining cypher as a legacy CLI alias.

Evaluation and ingest verification
- Queries canonical live relationship kinds and reports requested, canonical, and queried kinds for missing exact edges.
- Verifies all projected node types, including domain, GPO, container, and ADCS objects.
- Requires endpoint-anchored supporting-edge evidence and exact cardinality guards before direct or MCP grading.
- Classifies missing positive reference evidence as infrastructure failure rather than model failure.
- Preserves computed Cypher projections across WITH aggregation boundaries; regression coverage includes nodes(p) AS nodes.

Documentation and tests
- Updates the README and benchmark-products runbook with manifest v2 and relationship compatibility behavior.
- Adds relationship-registry, preflight, manifest, archive, grading, ingest-diagnostic, direct-alias, and computed-projection regression coverage.

